 coronary intervention</article-title><source>Am J Cardiol</source><year>2002</year><volume>89</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>586</fpage><lpage>589</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11867045</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b7-vhrm-5-275"><label>7.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kugelmass</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name><name><surname>Cohen</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Moscucci</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Elevation of the creatine kinase myocardial isoform following otherwise successful directional coronary atherectomy and stenting</article-title><source>Am J Cardiol</source><year>1994</year><volume>74</volume><issue>8</issue><fpage>748</fpage><lpage>754</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7942542</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b8-vhrm-5-275"><label>8.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wiviott</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Intensity of antiplatelet therapy in patients with acute coronary syndromes and percutaneous coronary intervention: the promise of prasugrel?</article-title><source>Cardiol Clin</source><year>2008</year><volume>26</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>629</fpage><lpage>637</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18929236</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b9-vhrm-5-275"><label>9.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Topol</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Toward a new frontier in myocardial reperfusion therapy: emerging platelet preeminence</article-title><source>Circulation</source><year>1998</year><volume>97</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>211</fpage><lpage>218</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9445175</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b10-vhrm-5-275"><label>10.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Coller</surname><given-names>BS</given-names></name><name><surname>Shattil</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The GPIIb/IIIa (integrin alphaIIbbeta3) odyssey: a technology-driven saga of a receptor with twists, turns, and even a bend</article-title><source>Blood</source><year>2008</year><volume>112</volume><issue>8</issue><fpage>3011</fpage><lpage>3025</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18840725</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b11-vhrm-5-275"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wiviott</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name><name><surname>Braunwald</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Angiolillo</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Greater clinical benefit of more intensive oral antiplatelet therapy with prasugrel in patients with diabetes mellitus in the trial to assess improvement in therapeutic outcomes by optimizing platelet inhibition with prasugrel-Thrombolysis in Myocardial Infarction 38</article-title><source>Circulation</source><year>2008</year><volume>118</volume><issue>16</issue><fpage>1626</fpage><lpage>1636</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18757948</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b12-vhrm-5-275"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schomig</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Neumann</surname><given-names>FJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Kastrati</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>A randomized comparison of antiplatelet and anticoagulant therapy after the placement of coronary-artery stents</article-title><source>N Engl J Med</source><year>1996</year><volume>334</volume><issue>17</issue><fpage>1084</fpage><lpage>1089</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8598866</pu